# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds the SQL Server login and the OpenAI key. Negation is last so an
# .env.example placeholder can still be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Detected database content ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rebuilt on demand by `python main.py --detect-only --refresh`, so nothing is
# lost by ignoring it. Kept out of git because it is not just structure:
# value_hints.txt holds REAL values sampled from the live lookup tables, and
# schema.txt names every column of a client database.
.cache/

# ── Run outputs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# slipped_wells.csv is live well data; the brief quotes real well ids and dates.
out/
out*/

# ── NOT ignored: sql/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The frozen, verified queries (app/frozen.py) are COMMITTED on purpose, and adding them here
# would quietly undo the point of freezing them. They are schema, not data - a SELECT naming
# columns, with no well ids or dates in it - and they are the artefact a reviewer reads to see
# what changed about how slippage is calculated. Committed, they also let a fresh clone serve
# the dashboard with no API key and no agent run at all.
#   sql/*.tmp is the atomic-write scratch file, which should never be committed.
sql/*.tmp

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Frontend (web/) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules is 384 MB across 11k files and .next is another 154 MB; both are
# rebuilt by `npm install` and `npm run build`. package-lock.json is deliberately
# NOT here - it pins the exact versions, so it belongs in the repo.
# NOTE: git does not support trailing comments - a `#` after a pattern becomes part
# of the pattern, so every comment here is on its own line.
node_modules/
.next/
# `next export` output; same name as the pipeline's out/, already ignored above.
# Regenerated by next on every dev/build:
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel/

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/

# ── Editors and OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Stray files from mistyped shell redirects (e.g. `2>0` instead of `2>&1`).
# Three of these got committed before being noticed; ignoring the shape stops it recurring.
0
ts.target_*
